Vulkan on Android: run without geometry shaders (Mali).

Blender-owned files; every hunk is enclosed in "UPBGE - Android" comments.

No shipped shader has a geometry stage: the Vulkan backend only injects one
to emulate a missing extension. Without geometry shader support:
- GHOST and the GPU backend no longer require the feature on Android;
- multi-viewport is off unless VK_EXT_shader_viewport_index_layer exists, so
  EEVEE renders shadow tiles into the largest viewport (existing fallback);
- materials using barycentrics (Wireframe, Geometry > Parametric) compile
  without them unless VK_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric exists
  (new GPU_shader_barycentric_support());
- the Gaussian splat shader declares the viewport output under the same
  condition as the mesh shader.

Applies after 0001 and 0002.

